<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghadames</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ghadamis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghadames is an oasis town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> near the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> held it as an outpost called Cydamus, and for centuries it was a key stop on trans-Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger bend</a>. Its old town of whitewashed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> houses with covered alleys is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghadames.jpg" alt="Ghadames" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghadames_Mosque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
